{
 "_doc": "Necromancer gear look props: which model shows which item. Consumed by DmGearModels (godot/game/dm_gear_models.gd) and DmAvatar. Prop GLBs are godot/assets/slice/models/props/<prop>.glb, built from art-manifest/tripo-specs/prop_necro_*.json. All props: +Y up, +X forward (the way the wearer faces), +Z is the left-right axis (mantle width, scythe/sickle blade sweep), mesh centred on the origin and normalised to about 1 unit on the longest axis (bounds below), so scale uniformly to length_m / bounds.size[1] (weapons), width_m / bounds.size[2] (mantles) or height_m / bounds.size[1] (helms). Weapons: place the prop so the point grip_t of the way up its Y extent (from bounds.min[1]) sits at the hand origin, long axis along the hand's up; tip is the +Y end. Mantles/helms: centre the prop on anchor_bone plus offset_m (metres, hero model space); weapons use length_m and grip_t (the shaft's measured position at that height is the grip); helms and mantles are sized from the head / chest measured on each rig (DmAvatar HELM_FIT, MANTLE_FIT), height_m / width_m / offset_m are only the fallback when a rig has no measurable head or chest.",
 "axes": {
  "up": "+Y",
  "forward": "+X",
  "side": "Z"
 },
